{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will harden.</b> One may ask: if HaShem hardened his heart, what was his offense, what was his sin? The answer is that HaShem gave wisdom to man and planted understanding in his heart to receive supernal power, to add to his good or to diminish his evil. This I will explain in [the portion of] Ki Tissa, and in the verse \"Who would grant that their heart be like this\" (Deuteronomy 5:26). Now the meaning of \"I will harden his heart, in order to multiply My signs\" — and Rabbi Yeshuah said that the meaning of \"I will harden his heart\" is to endure the plagues, and he did not speak correctly."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:15.947591706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}